// Verilator flags that are independent of the configuration

// Warnings
-Wall
-Wno-BLKANDNBLK
-Wno-CASEINCOMPLETE
-Wno-CMPCONST
-Wno-WIDTH
-Wno-WIDTHCONCAT
-Wno-UNSIGNED
-Wno-UNUSED
-Wno-UNOPTFLAT
// Continue despite warnings
// -Wno-fatal

// C++ mode and flags
--cc
-O3
-CFLAGS "-std=c++11 -Wall -g -O3"
-LDFLAGS "-pthread -lutil -lelf"

// Specifies the maximum number of loop iterations that may be unrolled.
// This is necessary for the SRAM model where we have blocking assignments in
// for loops, which only works if we unroll them.
--unroll-count 256

// Build the executable
--exe

// Control the size of the executable
--output-split 5000

// Evaluate the performance gain
// --threads 4

// Gain more insights on the signals that Verilator failed to optimize
// --report-unoptflat

// Build the model hierarchical. For MinPool, a non-hierarchical model might be faster
// Build the model hierarchical.
//
// MEASURED 2026-08-06, do not drop this without re-measuring: without it, verilating the
// 1024-core model reached 790 GB RSS (52% of a 1511 GB machine) after 2h53m and had not
// emitted a single .cpp -- the hierarchical build emits 11704 files in ~22 min. It had to
// be killed to protect concurrent simulations from the OOM killer.
//
// The 8x8 hierarchical model does link (1690 MB) but then segfaults: the per-group
// protectlib create call dereferences a null vlSymsp in the first initial block (64 calls
// at 8x8 vs 16 at 4x4). That is Verilator 4.228 codegen -- QuestaSim runs the same design,
// and it fails with ulimit -s unlimited so it is not a stack limit. The fix is Verilator
// 5.006/5.020 (installed on this host), NOT dropping --hierarchical.
--hierarchical

// Flush streams after each $display. The timing impact is usually nonmeasurable
--autoflush

// Set timescale to get consistent results with Modelsim/VCS
--timescale 1ns/1ns
